[medium] Possible null/undefined gap: this branch assumes both `asset.fileModifiedAt` and `asset.fileCreatedAt` are non-null `Date`s. If either can be null/undefined (or not a Date), the comparison here and the later `toISOString()` call can throw. Adding a guard would help (e.g., use whichever timestamp is available, falling back to `asset.createdAt` or `new Date(0)` as a last resort), and `localDateTime` should be confirmed to be a valid `Date` before logging.

```suggestion
      const created = asset.fileCreatedAt;
      const modified = asset.fileModifiedAt;
      const earliestDate = created && modified ? (modified < created ? modified : created) : (modified ?? created ?? asset.createdAt);
      if (!earliestDate) {
        this.logger.warn(`Asset ${asset.id} has no file timestamps; falling back to current time`);
        dateTimeOriginal = new Date();
        localDateTime = dateTimeOriginal;
      } else {
        dateTimeOriginal = earliestDate;
        localDateTime = earliestDate;
      }
```
